WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.868
Trump, who has said we should it.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.902
And you remember this.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.570
He used to say,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.605
I only hire the best people.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.506
He's blaming

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.073
Chris Christie

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.275
for the hiring of the FBI

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.210
director, Christopher Wright.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.644
Let's listen to this.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.848
Is it a mistake to put Christopher

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.715
Wray there?

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.717
Sadly, it probably was.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:17.917
You know,

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.352
he was recommended very strongly

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.987
by Chris Christie,

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.790
who was, you know, a sad case.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.325
I mean, I watch him. He's a sad case.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.259
Well, he's in this race.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.594
He said just to take you down.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.261
Well, I know.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.462
And you know how he's doing.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.797
He's at 1%

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.064
and he

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:31.731
probably won't

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.367
even make the debate stage.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:35.335
Yeah.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.170
Jason, I mean, what do you make of that?

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.772
I mean, Wray did come under attack

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.207
from many Republicans this past week.

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.009
Does this undermine

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:43.877
some of these claims

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.311
that they support law enforcement

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.413
when they go after Chris

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.180
Wray in that fashion?

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.548
And what about Trump

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.483
blaming this on Christie?

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.918
Well, I mean, two things down

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.485
package there.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:52.786
I think

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.287
first off, I think there is

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.790
the FBI does deserve some criticism

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.757
for how they've operated.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.759
I mean, the report came out.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.162
But I think that the law and order folks

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.063
on the day to day

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:05.732
job, the FBI folks are doing a great job.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.201
But I think the FBI still needs

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.403
there needs to be some,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.037
you know,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.939
I guess reconfigure nation

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.507
or addressing

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.008
the fact

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.043
that some of the cases went out too far.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.679
I think the Democrats said this in 2016

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.181
with what they did with Hillary Clinton.

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.315
I think Republicans are saying

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:23.616
that legitimately now

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.818
as far as you know

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.886
Chris Christie getting blamed for hiring

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.987
Chris Wray.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.023
That's ridiculous.

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:30.623
I mean

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.958
Chris Christie never had

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:32.826
hiring authority.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.128
He never had the ability to say

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.297
you should be hiring this person

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.398
and if you don't,

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.333
then you're going to go down the hill.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.669
I mean that all rests on Trump

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:43.570
and the other folks

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.804
in the administration.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.371
Yeah, Mollie,

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.207
I mean, this is another case of Trump

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.374
sort of disowning people

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.577
that he's hired over the years and put in

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:51.845
some pretty lofty positions

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.848
Yeah, I think it's a little

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.282
bit unfair to compare

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.717
what James Comey did

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.618
to Hillary Clinton

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.886
right before the election

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:03.156
with that letter to what the FBI

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:06.092
has tried to do with Republicans.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.661
I mean, that would Comey really was

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.163
I mean, he doesn't feel he did that,

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.064
but he really did

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.632
put his finger on the scale

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.801
there in a way that did really affect

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.169
the 2016 election.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:16.970
In fact,

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.303
you know,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.304
there's lots of reporting

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.739
that says Hillary might have won

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.307
had it not been for that letter.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.143
So I don't know that these two things are

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:23.610
the same.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.744
I would also say,

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:26.246
you know, Chris Wray is a Republican.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.648
The FBI has been run almost completely,

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.917
probably completely by Republicans,

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.719
you know, since its inception.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:35.555
I think that this is just a weird far

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.023
right talking point.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.091
I don't think that

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.392
there is much mainstream

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.661
support for disbanding the FBI

